  "content": {
    "id": "p22-q1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "On a winter’s day, the hourly temperature was recorded every hour for 24 hours, starting at 9 am. The maximum temperature was $14^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$ and occurred at 3 pm. The minimum temperature was $2^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$ and occurred at 3 am.\n\nThe temperature $T$ (in $^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$) can be modelled by the function:\n$$T(t)=b+a\\sin(nt),$$\nwhere $t$ is the number of hours after 9 am.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p22-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the values of $a$ and $b$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=6$, $b=8$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}a&=\\frac{14-2}{2}\\\\a&=6\\\\b&=\\frac{14+2}{2}\\\\b&=8\\end{align*}$$\nThe temperature rises from its mean at 9 am, so $a$ is positive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Sketch the graph of $T(t)$ over a 24-hour period starting at 9 am.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "A sine curve through $(0,8)$, $(6,14)$, $(12,8)$, $(18,2)$ and $(24,8)$.",
          "worked": "The mean temperature is $8^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$ and the amplitude is $6^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$. Draw a smooth sine curve through $(0,8)$, $(6,14)$, $(12,8)$, $(18,2)$ and $(24,8)$, rising initially.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p22-q1-b-solution-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"temperatureBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"temperature function\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 22 question 19F 1(b); teacher page 24\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.22cm,y=0.25cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{temperatureBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt] (0,0)--(26,0) node[right] {$t$};\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt] (0,0)--(0,16) node[above] {$T(t)$};\n\\foreach \\v in {6,12,18,24}{\\draw[line width=0.4pt] (\\v,0.2)--(\\v,-0.2);\\node[below] at (\\v,-0.2) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$\\v$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\node[below left] at (0,0) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$0$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n\\foreach \\v in {2,8,14}{\\draw[dashed,line width=0.4pt] (0,\\v)--(24,\\v);\\node[left] at (0,\\v) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$\\v$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};}\n\\draw[temperatureBlue,line width=0.8pt,domain=0:24,samples=121] plot (\\x,{8+6*sin(15*\\x)});\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 70,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 22,
                "sourceRegion": "19F 1(b); corresponding answer graph on teacher PDF page 24",
                "description": "One full temperature cycle with labelled quarter-period ticks and dashed minimum, mean and maximum guides.",
                "mathematics": "T(t)=8+6 sin(pi t/12), 0<=t<=24.",
                "answerVisibility": "Solution only; no supplied student graph."
              },
              "derived": false,
              "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
            }
          ]
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 65
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the period of the function. Hence, calculate $n$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Period: $24$ hours; $n=\\dfrac{\\pi}{12}$.",
          "worked": "The maximum and minimum occur 12 hours apart, which is half a period. The period is therefore 24 hours.\n$$\\begin{align*}24&=\\frac{2\\pi}{n}\\\\24n&=2\\pi\\\\n&=\\frac{\\pi}{12}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Find the temperature, correct to one decimal place, at 2 pm.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$13.8^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.",
          "worked": "At 2 pm, $t=5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}T(5)&=8+6\\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{12}\\right)\\\\T(5)&\\approx13.8\\end{align*}$$\nThe temperature is $13.8^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$, correct to one decimal place.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Find the times when the temperature is $11^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "11 am and 7 pm.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}8+6\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}\\right)&=11\\\\\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}\\right)&=\\frac12\\\\\\frac{\\pi t}{12}&=\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\quad\\text{or}\\quad\\frac{5\\pi}{6}\\\\t&=2\\quad\\text{or}\\quad10\\end{align*}$$\nThese are 11 am and 7 pm in the recorded 24-hour period.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      },
      {
        "id": "p22-q1-f",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "f",
        "prompt": "Find the times to the nearest minute when the temperature is $7^\\circ\\mathrm{C}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "9:38 pm and 8:22 am the following day.\n\nSolve $\\sin(\\pi \\frac{t}{12})=-\\frac{1}{6}$ in the recorded 24-hour period.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}8+6\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}\\right)&=7\\\\\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}\\right)&=-\\frac16\\end{align*}$$\nLet $\\alpha=\\arcsin(\\frac{1}{6})$. For $0\\le t\\le24$, the angle lies in the third or fourth quadrant.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{\\pi t}{12}&=\\pi+\\alpha\\quad\\text{or}\\quad2\\pi-\\alpha\\\\t&=12+\\frac{12\\alpha}{\\pi}\\quad\\text{or}\\quad24-\\frac{12\\alpha}{\\pi}\\\\t&\\approx12.6396\\quad\\text{or}\\quad23.3604\\end{align*}$$\nMeasured from 9 am, these times are 9:38 pm and 8:22 am the following day, to the nearest minute.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 43
      }
    ]
  },
